  "date": "01/08/09",
  "content": "I had a really bad pain in my solar plexus. I was screaming very loudly. When the emergency services took me to the hospital, they gave me shot after shot of painkillers, but my pain didn't go away. I was screaming as if I was crazy. The nurse mentioned that she had never ever heard somebody screaming like that. (My ex-boyfriend told me about it later). After six or seven shots of painkiller, I left my body. I was in the corner by the ceiling and watching my body lying on the bed and my boyfriend was sitting next to me. I felt profound joy and peace. I flew closer to my body and thought that I looked very pretty and young. When my boyfriend started to shake me, I returned to my body.",
